  "result": "If I could change the world in one way, I\u2019d give every person the ability to truly understand and feel another being\u2019s experience\u2014human or non-human alike. Imagine a world where, before passing judgment or drawing a boundary (between nations, faiths, species, political views), we could momentarily inhabit the feelings, fears, hopes and needs of someone else. \n\nSuch universal empathy would:\n\n \u2022 Dissolve the \u201cus vs. them\u201d mentality that fuels war, prejudice and social division.  \n \u2022 Shift policy-making toward cooperation\u2014on poverty, health care, climate, immigration\u2014because leaders would viscerally grasp how their decisions impact real lives.  \n \u2022 Transform education, business and science into truly collaborative enterprises, driven by concern for collective well-being instead of narrow self-interest.  \n \u2022 Extend moral consideration to animals and ecosystems, fostering responsible stewardship of the planet.\n\nWith empathy as our default lens, every other challenge\u2014inequality, environmental collapse, political polarization\u2014would suddenly become far easier to solve, because we\u2019d be motivated not by abstract ideals but by a shared, deeply felt connection to one another.",
